              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "scrīnium, scrīniī — \"a writing case, chest for papers\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Epistulās in scrīniō servō. I keep the letters in a writing case."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter, second declension. A round box for book-rolls and letters."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "scrīnium is a native Latin noun; Lewis & Short links it with scrībō \"to write\", but EtymDB traces it to a root meaning \"to cut\", so the origin is not settled. English shrine comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
