              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rescrībō, rescrībere — \"to write back, reply\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Epistulam tuam accēpī et statim rescrībō. I have received your letter and I am writing back at once."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rescrībō, rescrībere, rescrīpsī, rescrīptum. An emperor's written answer was a rescrīptum."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rescrībō is built on re- \"back\" and scrībō \"to write\" (Lewis & Short). English rescript comes from its participle."
            }
          ]
        },
